10. Food Waste Monitoring System

1. Problem Statement
Compare meals prepared, meals served, and leftovers over several days. Calculate waste percentages
and identify days where waste exceeds an acceptable threshold.

2. Objectives
•	Calculate leftover meals and waste percentage.
•	Compare daily waste against a threshold.
•	Summarize total waste over the period.

3. Assumptions
•	Meals prepared and served are non-negative integers.
•	Leftovers = prepared − served.
•	Waste percentage = leftovers / prepared × 100.
•	A day is flagged if waste percentage exceeds 10%; prepared meals must be greater than zero.

4. Algorithm
1. Store daily prepared and served counts in a list of tuples.
2. Calculate leftovers and percentage for each day.
3. Flag waste percentages above 10%.
4. Sum total prepared, served, and leftover meals.
5. Print daily and overall results.

